From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] igmp, mld: drop a report from a port the port db does not
 name

The IGMP report and leave paths and the MLD report and done handlers
pass portdb_get_ifname_from_portindex() of the receiving port to
l2mcd_is_peerlink() unchecked; receive_igmp_packet()'s own peer-link
test checks it. l2mcd_is_peerlink() makes a std::string of the name,
and NULL throws std::logic_error, which nothing catches: the daemon
aborts. A port index without a name is reached when a breakout numbers
a re-created port under another port's index and the name there is
then deleted, leaving that port's receive socket on the index.

Seen on a Celestica DX010 (SONiC 202511): l2mcd aborted on
"basic_string: construction from null is not valid" one second after a
port's link came back up at the index whose name a breakout had taken
(l2mcd's core: receive_igmp_packet() -> l2mcd_is_peerlink(), an IGMPv3
report on index 4096, which the port db held no name for). systemd
restarted it three minutes later.

receive_igmp_packet() and receive_mld_packet() now drop any message but
a query from such a port, counted in rx_bad_if and logged with the
VLAN's debug log, as a packet from a down port is. Queries take no
name on their way and are processed as before.
---
 src/igmp_io.c | 11 +++++++++++
 src/mld_io.c  | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/igmp_io.c b/src/igmp_io.c
index 867eb20..4827893 100644
--- a/src/igmp_io.c
+++ b/src/igmp_io.c
@@ -728,6 +728,17 @@ int receive_igmp_packet (IP_PARAMETERS  *sptr_ip_parameters)
             FN,LN, sptr_igmp_message->type, sptr_ip_parameters->rx_phy_port_number, portdb_get_ifname_from_portindex(sptr_ip_parameters->rx_phy_port_number),
             mcast_print_addr(&group_addr), dest_ip,clnt_src_ip);
     }
+    /* A report or leave from a port the port db does not name is dropped: the
+     * report and leave paths below pass the name to l2mcd_is_peerlink(), which
+     * makes a std::string of it, and NULL throws std::logic_error, which nothing
+     * catches. Such a port is one numbered under an index that has lost its name
+     * (a port re-created at another port's index); a query takes no name. */
+    if (!if_name && sptr_igmp_message->type != IGMP_MEMBERSHIP_QUERY_TYPE) {
+        L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_ERR(vid, "%s:%d:[vlan:%d] igmp_type:0x%x rx_port_num:%d: the port has no name in the port db. Dropping packet",
+            FN, LN, vid, sptr_igmp_message->type, sptr_ip_parameters->rx_phy_port_number);
+        igmp->rx_bad_if++;
+        goto free_packet;
+    }
 
     if (!MCGRP_IS_VALID_INTF(rx_port_number))
     {
diff --git a/src/mld_io.c b/src/mld_io.c
index fa5a9d7..dcdd972 100644
--- a/src/mld_io.c
+++ b/src/mld_io.c
@@ -1638,6 +1638,16 @@ int receive_mld_packet(IP6_RX_PKT_MSG *mld_pkt_msg)
     }
     mld_pkt_msg->ip_param.hopbyhop_length = hbh_len;
 
+    /* As in receive_igmp_packet(): the report and done handlers pass the port's
+     * name to l2mcd_is_peerlink(), and a NULL name throws std::logic_error. */
+    if (!ifname && icmp6h->type != MLD_MEMBERSHIP_QUERY_TYPE)
+    {
+        L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_ERR(vid, "%s:%d:[vlan:%d] mld_type:%d rx_port_num:%u: the port has no name in the port db. Dropping packet",
+                           FN, LN, vid, icmp6h->type, rx_phy_port);
+        mld->rx_bad_if++;
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     switch (icmp6h->type)
     {
     case MLD_MEMBERSHIP_QUERY_TYPE: // MLDv1v2 Query
